    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19727" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεβαι-ωτής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who gives assurance of</i> a thing,
			<i>authority</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφισβητουμένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.40.3
				</span></i>
			 (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστορίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.67
			</span></i>, al.; <i>confirmatory</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> legal
				<i>surety</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ μόνιμον τὴν ὁμόνοιαν γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.40.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. τῆς πίστεως παρέχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Flam.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; <i>warrantor</i> in sales, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2832
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Amphipolis</span>), etc.</div>
